==============================================================================================================
    splice at y = 2.337412405: C_L left = 0.006639363412, right = 0.006639363412
    dC_L/dy left = -0.036106062, right = -0.001361348, jump = 0.0347447
    min C_L on y in 1e-3..1e6: 3.238e-8
  [PASS] S5 C_L is continuous and positive at the splice and everywhere, and its derivative jumps there: h is C^{1,1} (not C^2), so Q(Z) = Z + 2 int h_mono is C^2 but not C^3
         measured: C_L jump 3.75e-27; C_L(splice) = 0.00663936; dC_L/dy -0.036106 -> -0.0013613; min C_L 3.24e-8
         reading:  strict convexity (XC5 E3) needs only C_L > 0; the jump in dC_L/dy leaves the cubic constitutive vertex without a unique value at y* -- a C^2 variant (smooth max) or nonsmooth analysis is XR3's step-0 (b) decision

